    "options": {
      "A": "Use the same cabbage extract for both, add comparable dropper amounts of each liquid, and record both final colours.",
      "B": "Use one drop of vinegar and ten drops of soap water; the test is still fair if the indicator is the same.",
      "C": "If both liquids can later be labelled acid or base, the comparison must have been fair no matter how it was done.",
      "D": "Different starting colours of vinegar and soap water make any comparison unfair, even if final colours are recorded clearly."
